makepad text layouter: a truncation ellipsis starts where the kept text ends, and the truncated row is aligned again (decision D10d).

`truncate_last_row_with_ellipsis` popped glyphs and placed the ellipsis from the row's `width_in_lpxs`. A soft-wrapped
row keeps the space it broke at as its last glyph (for caret positions) while `finish_current_row` leaves that space
out of the width, so popping it subtracted its advance a second time: the ellipsis was placed one space advance short
of the text, over the last glyph it kept. On a single-line wrapping Label (`max_lines: 1`, `text_overflow: Ellipsis`,
the Label's default `Flow::right_wrap()`) whose bound kept that space but not the next grapheme, "Fix steer queue
drop…" read "Fix steer queue drop.." (live: the ellipsis at x=132.631 in a 145.811 px label, the "p" ending at 136.568;
the first dot inside the "p", the third well inside the label, so clipping was never the cause). The truncation now
counts from the pen (the last glyph's origin + advance) before it pops.

A row's `origin_in_lpxs.x` (from `align`) was computed from its width before truncation changed it; it is now
computed again from the truncated width (an overflowing centred non-wrapping row was left at a negative origin, its
first glyphs outside the bound).

Unit tests: ellipsis_after_a_soft_wrap_space_starts_where_the_text_ends, ellipsis_row_geometry_holds_at_every_bound
(a sweep of bounds: wrap and no wrap, one and two rows) and a_truncated_aligned_row_is_placed_inside_its_bound.
Applied to every tree by scripts/apply-makepad-patches.sh; tests/a32_makepad_ellipsis.rs checks its shape.

